   "evidence": "`def IsSignedTransverseZero (\u03c3 : \u2200 z, L z) (x : X) (s : Bool) : Prop := \u2203 D c, HasFDerivAt (negPointTwistChartReading \u2102 x \u03c3) D (chartAt \u2102 x x) \u2227 \u2016D - (...).smulRight c\u2016 < \u2016c\u2016`. There is no `\u03c3 x = 0` conjunct, and `exists_untwist_section_of_finset` gets `\u03c3 x = 0` separately from `hZ`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Holomorphic/PointTwist/Divisor.lean",
   "fix": "Say that the predicate constrains only the derivative of the chart reading at `x`, and that vanishing at `x` is a separate hypothesis (as in `hZ` of `exists_untwist_section_of_finset`). Alternatively, add `\u03c3 x = 0` to the definition. Fix the Main definitions bullet to match.",
   "issue": "The docstring opens 'A zero `x` of `\u03c3` is transverse of sign `s` when\u2026', and the module's Main definitions list calls it 'a zero of a section which is positive or negative'. The definition only asks for the derivative estimate and never requires `\u03c3 x = 0`. It also holds at non-zeros: a chart reading `w \u21a6 w - \u03c6 x + 1` with `c = 1` satisfies it. Readers will wrongly expect `IsSignedTransverseZero \u03c3 x s \u2192 \u03c3 x = 0`.",
   "line": 280
  }
